      "comment": "A 10 kg shaft turning at 100 rad/s in a plain journal bearing of 25 mm radius, 25 mm long, with a radial clearance of 50 um and oil of 5 mPa s, its axis horizontal (the bearing's frame is turned so that its z axis is along the shaft). Released concentric, the shaft sinks and settles where the oil film carries its weight: an eccentricity ratio of about 0.6, with the journal displaced to one side of the load line (the attitude angle of the short bearing, tan(phi) = pi sqrt(1 - e^2) / (4 e)). The eccentricity ratio, the minimum film thickness, the peak film pressure, the friction torque and the oil flow are logged.",
